STATEMENT OF CHANGES (Apache-2.0 §4(b))
---------------------------------------

These files have been MODIFIED from their upstream form. fabius bundles them as
a reference corpus, not as a redistribution of the upstream project, and the
changes are naming-level rather than functional:

  * The project name "HyperFrames" was rewritten to "fabius-frames" across
    directory names, file names and documentation prose, so text and paths here
    will not match upstream.
  * Some in-code identifiers and repository URLs were rewritten by the same
    pass. Some rewritten URLs and package names no longer resolve upstream —
    treat every link and install command in this corpus as unverified, and
    prefer the upstream project for anything you intend to run.
  * Claims about the upstream project (production use, adopters, community
    examples) belong to HyperFrames/HeyGen, not to fabius.
  * Upstream copyright notices and license headers are retained wherever they
    were present; none were deliberately removed.

Nothing here is relicensed. This material keeps its upstream Apache-2.0 terms in
both directions — fabius's own license does not extend to it, and its license
does not extend to fabius. For anything you intend to USE rather than read, go
to the upstream project.
